# data-flow-architecture

## Core Data Flow Components
Importance Score: 85/100

1. Career Document Processing Pipeline
- Input documents flow through specialized chunking system
- Career context tokens extracted and embedded into vector store
- Document chunks processed with 1500 char/200 overlap optimization
- Output routed to tenant-specific storage contexts

2. Multi-tenant Context Management Flow
- User requests isolated into separate processing streams
- Career context data flows through dedicated tenant channels
- Version control system manages context state transitions
- Dynamic context routing based on user session state

3. Retrieval Integration Pipeline
- Semantic search queries flow through career-optimized filters
- Top 5 relevant chunks assembled into context window
- Professional tone markers injected into generation stream
- Context-aware prompts combined with retrieval results

## Data Flow Patterns

1. Document Processing Flow
```
Raw Document → Context Extraction → Chunk Processing → Vector Embedding → Tenant Storage
```

2. Context Management Flow
```
User Request → Tenant Isolation → Context Loading → Version Check → Agent Instantiation
```

3. Retrieval Pipeline Flow
```
Query → Semantic Search → Context Assembly → Prompt Integration → Generation
```

## Critical Data Isolation Points

1. Career Context Boundaries
- Complete separation of user document spaces
- Isolated vector stores per tenant
- Independent context version tracking
- Tenant-specific prompt customization

2. Processing Stream Isolation
- Dedicated processing queues per tenant
- Isolated career context caching
- Separate retrieval indices
- Independent generation pipelines

